  "text": "```verilog\nmodule afifo #(\n\tparameter LGFIFO = 3,\n\tparameter WIDTH  = 16,\n\tparameter NFF    = 2,\n\tparameter [0:0] WRITE_ON_POSEDGE = 1'b1,\n\tparameter [0:0] OPT_REGISTER_READS = 1'b1\n) (\n\tinput\twire\t\t\ti_wclk, i_wr_reset_n, i_wr,\n\tinput\twire\t[WIDTH-1:0]\ti_wr_data,\n\toutput\treg\t\t\to_wr_full,\n\tinput\twire\t\t\ti_rclk, i_rd_reset_n, i_rd,\n\toutput\treg\t[WIDTH-1:0]\to_rd_data,\n\toutput\treg\t\t\to_rd_empty\n);\n\n\tlocalparam DEPTH = 1 << LGFIFO;\n\tlocalparam MASK  = DEPTH - 1;\n\n\t// Write Pointer (Gray Code)\n\treg [LGFIFO-1:0] wr_gray;\n\treg [LGFIFO-1:0] wr_gray_next;\n\treg [LGFIFO-1:0] wr_ptr;\n\n\t// Read Pointer (Gray Code)\n\treg [LGFIFO-1:0] rd_gray;\n\treg [LGFIFO-1:0] rd_gray_next;\n\treg [LGFIFO-1:0] rd_ptr;\n\n\t// Counters for Full/Empty logic\n\treg [LGFIFO-1:0] wr_cnt;\n\treg [LGFIFO-1:0] rd_cnt;\n\n\t// FIFO Memory\n\treg [WIDTH-1:0] mem [DEPTH-1:0];\n\n\t// Write Side Logic\n\talways @(posedge i_wclk or negedge i_wr_reset_n) begin\n\t\tif (!i_wr_reset_n) begin\n\t\t\twr_gray <= {1'b0, 1'b0};\n\t\t\twr_cnt  <= 0;\n\t\t\to_wr_full <= 1'b0;\n\t\tend else if (i_wr) begin\n\t\t\t// Calculate next Gray code\n\t\t\twr_gray_next = wr_gray;\n\t\t\twr_gray_next[0] = wr_gray[0] ^ wr_gray[1];\n\t\t\twr_gray_next[1] = wr_gray[1] ^ wr_gray[2];\n\t\t\t// ... propagate XOR for all bits\n\t\t\tfor (integer i = 2; i < LGFIFO; i = i + 1) begin\n\t\t\t\twr_gray_next[i] = wr_gray[i] ^ wr_gray[i+1];\n\t\t\tend\n\n\t\t\t// Update counter\n\t\t\tif (wr_cnt < MASK) begin\n\t\t\t\twr_cnt <= wr_cnt + 1;\n\t\t\tend\n\n\t\t\t// Update Gray code pointer based on counter\n\t\t\tif (wr_cnt == 0) begin\n\t\t\t\twr_gray <= wr_gray_next;\n\t\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\t\twr_gray <= wr_gray_next;\n\t\t\tend\n\n\t\t\t// Write data\n\t\t\tmem[wr_cnt] <= i_wr_data;\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t// Full flag: (wr_cnt + NFF) >= DEPTH\n\t\t\t// Using unsigned comparison\n\t\t\to_wr_full <= (wr_cnt + NFF) >= DEPTH;\n\t\tend\n\tend\n\n\t// Read Side Logic\n\talways @(posedge i_rclk or negedge i_rd_reset_n) begin\n\t\tif (!i_rd_reset_n) begin\n\t\t\trd_gray <= {1'b0, 1'b0};\n\t\t\trd_cnt  <= 0;\n\t\t\to_rd_empty <= 1'b1;\n\t\t\to_rd_data  <= 0;\n\t\tend else if (i_rd) begin\n\t\t\t// Calculate next Gray code\n\t\t\trd_gray_next = rd_gray;\n\t\t\trd_gray_next[0] = rd_gray[0] ^ rd_gray[1];\n\t\t\tfor (integer i = 2; i < LGFIFO; i = i + 1) begin\n\t\t\t\trd_gray_next[i] = rd_gray[i] ^ rd_gray[i+1];\n\t\t\tend\n\n\t\t\t// Update counter\n\t\t\tif (rd_cnt < MASK) begin\n\t\t\t\trd_cnt <= rd_cnt + 1;\n\t\t\tend\n\n\t\t\t// Update Gray code pointer based on counter\n\t\t\tif (rd_cnt == 0) begin\n\t\t\t\trd_gray <= rd_gray_next;\n\t\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\t\trd_gray <= rd_gray_next;\n\t\t\tend\n\n\t\t\t// Read data\n\t\t\tif (OPT_REGISTER_READS) begin\n\t\t\t\to_rd_data <= mem[rd_cnt];\n\t\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\t\to_rd_data <= mem[rd_cnt];\n\t\t\tend\n\n\t\t\t// Empty flag: (rd_cnt + NFF) <= wr_cnt\n\t\t\t// Using unsigned comparison\n\t\t\to_rd_empty <= (rd_cnt + NFF) <= wr_cnt;\n\t\tend\n\tend\n\n\t// Cross-domain synchronization for pointers to generate stable flags\n\t// We need to compare the Gray-coded pointers across domains.\n\t// Since we are using Gray codes, we can compare them directly if we ensure\n\t// the comparison logic is stable. However, standard practice is to use\n\t// a synchronizer chain for the pointers themselves or use a specific\n\t// cross-domain pointer comparison module.\n\t// Given the constraints of a single file and standard Verilog, we will implement\n\t// a simple pointer synchronizer for the read side to determine full,\n\t// and a pointer synchronizer for the write side to determine empty.\n\t// Actually, the standard efficient way is to synchronize the pointers\n\t// from the other domain.\n\n\t// Synchronize Write Pointer (from Write domain) to Read domain for Empty check\n\t// We need to pass wr_ptr (binary) or wr_gray (gray) to read domain.\n\t// Let's use the binary counter for comparison as it's easier to reason about levels,\n\t// but we must convert Gray to Binary in the write domain and send it, OR\n\t// convert Binary to Gray in the read domain and compare with Gray.\n\t// The most robust method for FIFOs is to send the Binary pointer from Write to Read\n\t// and Gray pointer from Read to Write, then convert in the respective domains.\n\t// However, to keep it simple and correct within one file without extra modules:\n\t// We will synchronize the WR pointer (binary) to the RD domain to calculate Empty.\n\t// And synchronize the RD pointer (binary) to the WR domain to calculate Full.\n\n\t// Synchronizers for Write Pointer (Binary) to Read Domain\n\treg [LGFIFO-1:0] wr_ptr_sync_1;\n\treg [LGFIFO-1:0] wr_ptr_sync_2;\n\n\talways @(posedge i_rclk or negedge i_rd_reset_n) begin\n\t\tif (!i_rd_reset_n) begin\n\t\t\twr_ptr_sync_1 <= 0;\n\t\t\twr_ptr_sync_2 <= 0;\n\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\twr_ptr_sync_1 <= wr_cnt;\n\t\t\twr_ptr_sync_2 <= wr_ptr_sync_1;\n\t\tend\n\tend\n\n\t// Synchronizers for Read Pointer (Binary) to Write Domain\n\treg [LGFIFO-1:0] rd_ptr_sync_1;\n\treg [LGFIFO-1:0] rd_ptr_sync_2;\n\n\talways @(posedge i_wclk or negedge i_wr_reset_n) begin\n\t\tif (!i_wr_reset_n) begin\n\t\t\trd_ptr_sync_1 <= 0;\n\t\t\trd_ptr_sync_2 <= 0;\n\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\trd_ptr_sync_1 <= rd_cnt;\n\t\t\trd_ptr_sync_2 <= rd_ptr_sync_1;\n\t\tend\n\tend\n\n\t// Final Full/Empty Logic using synchronized pointers\n\t// Full: (wr_cnt + NFF) >= rd_ptr_sync_2\n\t// Empty: (rd_cnt + NFF) <= wr_ptr_sync_2\n\n\t// Note: The internal o_wr_full and o_rd_empty in the pointer logic blocks above\n\t// were based on the local counters. We need to override them with the cross-domain\n\t// logic for the actual output ports, or restructure.\n\t// The requirement says \"Honor the full/empty flags\".\n\t// The standard approach:\n\t// 1. Calculate local flags based on local pointers (for reset behavior and immediate feedback).\n\t// 2. Use synchronized pointers for the final output flags to ensure stability across domains.\n\t// However, the prompt implies the outputs are the flags.\n\t// Let's refine: The outputs o_wr_full and o_rd_empty must be stable across domains.\n\t// Therefore, we calculate them using the synchronized pointers.\n\n\t// Re-evaluating the always blocks for outputs:\n\t// The previous always blocks updated o_wr_full/o_rd_empty based on local counters.\n\t// This is incorrect for cross-domain stability. The outputs must be driven by the\n\t// synchronized pointers.\n\t// We will move the output logic to separate processes or update the existing ones\n\t// to use the synchronized values.\n\n\t// Let's rewrite the output logic to use synchronized pointers.\n\t// Full: Write domain sees if (wr_cnt + NFF) >= rd_ptr_sync_2\n\t// Empty: Read domain sees if (rd_cnt + NFF) <= wr_ptr_sync_2\n\n\t// We need to update the output assignments.\n\t// Since o_wr_full and o_rd_empty are regs, we can assign them in the clock processes\n\t// using the synchronized values.\n\n\t// Update Write Side Output Logic\n\talways @(posedge i_wclk or negedge i_wr_reset_n) begin\n\t\tif (!i_wr_reset_n) begin\n\t\t\to_wr_full <= 1'b0;\n\t\tend else if (i_wr) begin\n\t\t\t// Full if (wr_cnt + NFF) >= synchronized_rd_ptr\n\t\t\to_wr_full <= (wr_cnt + NFF) >= rd_ptr_sync_2;\n\t\tend\n\tend\n\n\t// Update Read Side Output Logic\n\talways @(posedge i_rclk or negedge i_rd_reset_n) begin\n\t\tif (!i_rd_reset_n) begin\n\t\t\to_rd_empty <= 1'b1;\n\t\tend else if (i_rd) begin\n\t\t\t// Empty if (rd_cnt + NFF) <= synchronized_wr_ptr\n\t\t\to_rd_empty <= (rd_cnt + NFF) <= wr_ptr_sync_2;\n\t\tend\n\tend\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>\n<|endoftext|>",
